$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of alcohol (R)-9 (300 mg, 1.27 mmol, 1.00 eq.) in DMSO (10 mL)
in the presence of 4 Å (700 mg) was treated with IBX (533 mg, 1.90 mmol,
1.50 eq.) at rt and stirred at rt for 2 h The reaction was quenched by
addition of brine (40 mL) at rt and the aq. phase extracted with MTBE (4
× 40 mL). The combined organic extracts were washed with sat. aq. NaHCO3
solution (40 mL) and brine (40 mL), dried over MgSO4 and the solvent was
evaporated in vacuo. Column chromatography on silica gel (petroleum
ether/MTBE = 10:1). Aldehyde (R)-8 as a colorless oil (233 mg, 994 μmol,
78%). (2R)-(5-Methoxy-2,7-dimethylchroman-2-yl)-acetaldehyde (R-8)
Analytical data of aldehyde (R)-8: Optical Rotation: [α]D = ‒21.0 (c =
0.50, CHCl3, 25.1 °C). 1H-NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) = 1.40 (s, 3 H,
2'-CH3), 1.83 (dt, J = 14.1, 6.8 Hz, 1 H, 3'-Ha), 1.89 (dt, J = 14.1, 6.8
Hz, 1 H, 3'-Hb), 2.28 (s, 3 H, 7'-CH3), 2.57 (dd, J = 15.2, 3.1 Hz, 1 H,
2-Ha), 2.62 (t, J = 6.8 Hz, 2 H, 4'-Ha, 4'-Hb), 2.71 (dd, J = 15.2, 2.2
Hz, 1 H, 2-Hb), 3.80 (s, 3 H, 5'-OMe), 6.26, 6.31 (2 × s, 2 H, 6'-H,
8'-H), 9.89 (t, J = 2.7 Hz, 1 H, 1-H). 13C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm)
= 16.4 (C-4'), 21.6 (7'-CH3), 24.7 (2'-CH3), 32.3 (C-3'), 52.2 (C-2),
55.3 (5'-OMe), 74.2 (C-2'), 103.1, 110.3 (C-6', C-8'), 106.6 (C-4a'),
137.4 (C-7'), 153.4 (C-5'), 157.6 (C-8a'), 201.6 (C-1). IR (ATR): ν
(cm-1) = 2938, 2853, 1723, 1619, 1586, 1463, 1353, 1231, 1108, 816. UV
(CH3CN): λmax (nm) (lg ε) = 207.0 (4.634), 271.5 (2.951), 280.0 (2.937).
MS (ESI): m/z (%) = 235.1 (100) [M+H]+, 257.1 (31) [M+Na]+. C14H18O3
(234.29) calc.: 235.1329 found: 235.1330 [M+H]+ (ESI-HRMS).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, molecular sieves used (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
